Syncplay Droid 0.4.2

This product implements protocol behavior derived from and compatible with Syncplay and the
syncplay-noir fork, both distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Syncplay authors and contributors:
- Initial concept and core internals: Uriziel
- GUI design and lead development: Et0h
- Original SyncPlay code: Tomasz Kowalczyk (Fluxid)
- Other Syncplay contributors

This product uses AndroidX libraries for its user interface and Android platform integration,
Gson, Kotlin, and kotlinx.coroutines. It also uses SMBJ (com.hierynomus:smbj), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, and mpv-android-lib (io.github.abdallahmehiz:mpv-android-lib) as its
sole media playback engine. The mpv-android-lib Kotlin/JNI wrapper is MIT-licensed; its bundled
mpv, FFmpeg, libass, and related native components remain under their respective upstream
licenses, including GPL-licensed components. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
